        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0435" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg339"/>

                <head>No. 167.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Cadwalader.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 31, 1874</date>.
                        (Received October 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 802.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a copy of a letter which I have addressed to the legation, covering an
                    identical note from myself and several of my colleagues to our respective
                    superiors, in regard to the neutrality of the foreign settlements in China and
                    Japan in case of war, and to the immunity of our commerce.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Assistant
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d169-a1.xml" xpointer="d169-a1"/>
